title: Axel Leitner, 24, a student.
new-page: true
go-to: three

Axel Leitner, your roommate and comrade. 

You were similar, kind of. Both of you were ?"!, you were a Communist by circumstance as was he, just, differently. 

He was a middle class boy made poor boy by cirucmstance when he was doing his studies. He wanted to be a lawyer, you think, your memory is always awful, always has been.

You once were so sure your sister had died. You remembered her funeral...You thought you saw a ghost when she came home for your 13th Birthday. 

Your family thought you were playing a cruel joke. As you described, in such odd detail, the funeral, the tears, the eulogy.

Suffice to say, on that day, that happy day, you weren't fed. You were sent to your room. It was dark and cold.

Axel would never have done that, he had a memory sharp as a diamond. He was so quick witted, a real meritable man.

He was proof meritocracy didn't exist, if it did, you ought well known he'd be the man in charge. 

For he was perfect. Perfect requires a bit of oddness, humility. Yet always overcame with his charming handsomeness.

 You weren't. He was industrious, diligent... You weren't. No, you weren't at all. He was perfect with a dash of humility.

You were...

You were.......

You were...A sloth, a slug compared to him, that's what they always said, wasn't it? A rotting slug not fit to be squished beneath a jackboot.

Without humility. Without perfection. Without a oddness to be redeemed. You? You were just...a freak. A nonsenical freak. 

They weren't wrong, were they? They were always saying it, forever and ever, always, resounding in your head, in your sleep, in your wake.

But Axel didn't view you like that, you didn't think. Maybe he did now, with that. Your hand insctively went to stroke your neck, you did that a lot, it was a compulsion.

You brushed against your !?"4'! $%*"%! and wanted to be sick. You threw your head back. **Mistake.** You felt it grow and push against your skin. That feeling spread across your body, intensifying as you felt a snake slithering in your gut.

You felt hands grasp you all over, they were touching, grabbing you in every direction. You wanted to scream, again, but you couldn't disturb Axel. So you took it.

